hadiths[153]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That servant has failed and is in loss in whose heart Allah Almighty has not placed mercy for human beings."
"3206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Khalid bin al-Walid is one of the swords of Allah."
"3207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Khalid bin al-Walid is one of the swords of Allah; Allah has drawn him against the polytheists."
"3208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Khalid is one of the swords of Allah, and he is the finest young man of his tribe."
"3209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Oppose the polytheists: trim your moustaches closely and let your beards grow."
"3210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Oppose the Jews, for they do not pray in their sandals or their leather socks."
"3211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Lord informed me that I would see a sign in my Ummah, and that when I see it I should say abundantly: 'Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi, astaghfirullaha wa atubu ilayh' (Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him; I seek Allah's forgiveness and turn to Him in repentance). And I have seen that sign: 'When the help of Allah and the victory come' - that is, the conquest of Makkah - 'and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in multitudes, then glorify the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance.'"
"3212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Put your garment on, and do not walk about naked."
"3213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn the Qur'an from these four: Ibn Mas'ud, Ubayy bin Ka'b, Mu'adh bin Jabal, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah."
"3214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take your shield against the Fire: say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'Wal-hamdu lillah' (and praise be to Allah), 'Wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is no god but Allah) and 'Wallahu akbar' (and Allah is the Greatest), for these words will come on the Day of Resurrection as protectors in front, behind, and on the right and the left, and they are the enduring good deeds (al-baqiyat al-salihat)."
"3215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take it from me, take it from me: Allah Almighty has appointed a way for them. For the unmarried with the unmarried, the ruling is one hundred lashes and exile for a year; and for the married with the married, the ruling is one hundred lashes and stoning."
"3216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep to your places, for the people have prayed and gone to their beds, and you will continue to be counted as in prayer as long as you are waiting for the prayer. Were it not for the weakness of the weak, the sickness of the sick and the need of those in need, I would have delayed this prayer until the middle of the night."
"3217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take on as much worship as you are able to, for Allah does not tire of rewarding until you yourselves grow tired of doing deeds."
"3218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take on as many deeds as you are able to, for Allah does not grow weary until you yourselves grow weary."
"3219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Carry on with your play, O Banu Arfidah, so that the Jews and the Christians may know that there is latitude in our religion."
"3220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take a piece of cloth scented with musk and purify yourself with it."
"3221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take from his wealth, in a reasonable manner, what is sufficient for you and your sons."
"3222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from among those who came before you was walking proudly in a fine garment of his, so Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he will go on sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection."
"3223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was born through marriage, not through fornication, from the time of Adam (peace be upon him)."
"3224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was born through marriage, not through fornication."
"3225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was born through marriage, not through fornication, from the time of Adam (peace be upon him) until my parents gave birth to me; nothing of the fornication of the Jahiliyyah touched me."
"3226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I came out intending to inform you about Laylat al-Qadr, but two men quarrelled with each other, so this knowledge was taken away from me. So seek it in the last ten nights: on the seventh remaining, the ninth remaining, or the fifth remaining night."
"3227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The appearance of the signs of the Hour, one after another, will be continuous, just as beads on a string follow one after another."
"3228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The means for my Ummah to control their desires is fasting and standing in night prayer."
"3229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two traits never come together in a hypocrite: good conduct and understanding of the religion."
"3230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two practices which no Muslim servant keeps up without entering Paradise. Indeed, they are easy, yet those who act upon them are few: that he says Subhan Allah ten times after every prayer, Alhamdulillah ten times and Allahu akbar ten times - that makes one hundred and fifty on the tongue and fifteen hundred in the Scale; and that when he goes to his bed he says Allahu akbar thirty-four times, Alhamdulillah thirty-three times and Subhan Allah thirty-three times - that makes one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the Scale. So which of you commits two thousand five hundred sins in a day and a night?"
"3231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The recitation of the Qur'an (the Psalms) was made easy for Dawud (peace be upon him). He would order his mounts to be saddled, and he would finish reciting the Qur'an (the Psalms) before his mounts were saddled; and he ate nothing except from the earnings of his own hands."
"3232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have left behind among you two things, after which you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, and these two will never separate until they come to me at the Pond (al-Hawd)."
"3233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty created Adam (peace be upon him) in His special form, and his height was sixty cubits. Then He said: 'Go and greet those people' - they were a group of angels sitting there - 'and listen to how they reply to you, for that will be your greeting and the greeting of your offspring.' So he went and said: 'As-salamu alaykum (peace be upon you).' They replied: 'As-salamu alayka wa rahmatullah (peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah),' so they added 'wa rahmatullah'. So everyone who enters Paradise will be in the form of Adam (peace be upon him), sixty cubits tall, and since then the stature of creation has kept decreasing until now."
"3234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty created Adam (peace be upon him), then struck his right shoulder and brought out from it white offspring as though they were milk; then He struck his left shoulder and brought out from it black offspring as though they were charcoal. Then He said: 'These are for Paradise, and I do not care; and these are for Hell, and I do not care.'"
"3235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty created the soil on Saturday, created the mountains in it on Sunday, created the trees on Monday, created disliked things on Tuesday, created light on Wednesday, spread the animals in it on Thursday, and created Adam (peace be upon him) after Asr on Friday, at the end of creation, in the last of the hours of Friday, between Asr and nightfall."
"3236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty created mercy in one hundred parts. He placed one mercy among His creation, by which they show mercy to one another, and He kept ninety-nine with Himself."
"3237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty created Yahya bin Zakariyya (peace be upon him) a believer in his mother's womb, and created Pharaoh a disbeliever in his mother's womb."
"3238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels were created from light, the jinn were created from a flame of fire, and Adam (peace be upon him) was created from that which has been described to you."
"3239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pass your fingers between the fingers of your hands and the toes of your feet."
"3240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five things are tied to five things: no people broke a covenant but their enemy was given power over them; no people judged by other than what Allah revealed but poverty became widespread among them; no people among whom indecency spread but death became widespread among them; no people gave short measure and weight but produce was withheld from them and they were seized with years of famine; and no people withheld zakah but the rain was withheld from them."
"3241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five rights are due from a Muslim to his brother: returning the greeting of salam, responding to one who sneezes, accepting an invitation, visiting the sick, and following the funeral procession."
"3242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has made five prayers obligatory. Whoever performs the ablution for them well, offers them at their proper times, and completes their bowing and their humility, has a promise from Allah that He will forgive him; and whoever does not do so has no promise from Allah: if He wills, He will forgive him, and if He wills, He will punish him."
"3243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has prescribed five prayers for His servants. Whoever performs them without wasting any of them out of neglect of their right has a promise with Allah that He will admit him into Paradise; and whoever does not perform them has no promise with Allah: if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will admit him into Paradise."
"3244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five harmful creatures may be killed both outside and inside the Haram: the snake, the pied crow, the mouse, the biting dog, and the kite."
"3245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five creatures are lawful to kill in the Haram: the snake, the scorpion, the kite, the mouse, and the biting dog."
"3246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five harmful creatures which even a person in ihram may kill, and which may be killed within the Haram: the mouse, the scorpion, the snake, the biting dog, and the crow."
"3247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no expiation for five sins: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul unjustly, slandering a believer, fleeing from the battlefield, and a false oath by which someone's wealth is seized unjustly."
"3248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five harmful creatures which may be killed within the Haram: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the biting dog."
"3249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five creatures for the killing of which there is no sin upon a person in ihram: the crow, the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, and the biting dog."
"3250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five things are part of the fitrah (natural disposition): circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit hair."
"3251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim has five rights over a Muslim: returning his greeting, accepting his invitation, attending his funeral, visiting him when he is ill, and responding to him when he sneezes and says Alhamdulillah."
"3252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Five deeds: whoever does them in a single day, Allah records him among the people of Paradise: whoever fasts on the day of Friday, goes to the Friday prayer, visits a sick person, attends a funeral, and frees a slave."
"3253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five deeds; whoever does even one of them is under the guarantee of Allah: whoever visits a sick person, or sets out to fight in the path of Allah, or goes to his ruler intending to honour and respect him, or stays sitting in his house so that people are safe from his harm and he is safe from the harm of people."
"3254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five deaths such that whoever dies in any one of them is a martyr: the one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who drowns in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of a stomach illness in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of plague in the path of Allah is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth in the path of Allah is a martyr."
"3255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are five things which no one knows except Allah: Indeed, with Allah alone is the knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"3256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover the vessels, tie up the mouths of the waterskins, close the doors, and keep your children with you in the evening, for at that time the jinn spread out and snatch away; and put out the lamps when you go to sleep, for sometimes a mouse may drag the wick and burn the people of the house."
"3257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The caliphate of prophethood is thirty years; then Allah Almighty grants kingship to whomever He wills."
"3258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your rulers are those whom you love and who love you, for whom you pray and who pray for you; and the worst of your rulers are those whom you hate and who hate you, whom you curse and who curse you."
"3259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who have the best character."
"3260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who have the best character, who are gentle and courteous; and the worst of you are those who talk excessively, who boast, and who twist their tongues in speech."
"3261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who are best in repaying debts."
"3262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those whose lives are longest and whose character is best."
"3263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those whose lives are longest and whose deeds are best."
"3264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who are gentlest with their shoulders when forming the rows in prayer."
"3265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who are best to their wives."
"3266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who is best to his family."
"3267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you in the Days of Ignorance are also the best in Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion."
"3268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who learned the Qur'an and taught it to others."
"3269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your best names are Abdullah, Abdur-Rahman and al-Harith."
"3270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbours in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbour."
"3271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best places are the mosques and the worst places are the markets."
"3272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the Tabi'in is Uways (al-Qarani)."
"3273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best horse is one that is black, with a white blaze on the forehead and a white mark on the nose, with white on three legs while the right leg is free of markings; and if it is not black, then a reddish-brown horse with these same markings is the best."
"3274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best supplication is the supplication on the day of Arafah, and the best words that I and the prophets before me have said are: 'La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir' (There is no true god except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things)."
"3275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best provision is that which is just sufficient."
"3276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best testimony is that which the witness gives before he is asked for it."
"3277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best witness is the one who gives his testimony before he is asked for it."
"3278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best travelling party consists of four people, the best detachment consists of four hundred, the best army consists of four thousand, and an army of twelve thousand will never be defeated on account of small numbers."
"3279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best dowry (mahr) is the one that is easiest."
"3280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that which leaves the giver well-off; the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and when giving charity, begin with those whom you support."
"3281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that which is given from surplus wealth; and begin with those whom you support."
"3282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best deed is that you depart from this world while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah."
"3283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best earning is the earning of the worker's own hand, when he works with sincerity."
"3284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best speech is four phrases, and it does not harm you with which of them you begin: 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'wal-hamdu lillah' (and praise be to Allah), 'wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is no god but Allah) and 'wallahu akbar' (and Allah is the Greatest)."
"3285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best gathering is the one that is most spacious."
"3286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe."
"3287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are those who have the best character."
"3288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are those of my era, then the second era, then the third era."
"3289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are those who are most beneficial to people."
"3290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are those who are best in repaying debts."
"3291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best person is the one whose heart is pure and whose tongue is truthful."" It was asked: ""What is a pure heart?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is the God-fearing, pure heart in which there is no sin, no transgression and no envy."" It was asked: ""Then who comes after him?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is averse to this world and loves the Hereafter."" It was asked: ""Then who comes after him?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer with good character."
"3292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best person in times of trials is a man who holds the reins of his horse, pursuing the enemies of Allah, frightening them while they frighten him; or a man who lives in seclusion in the wilderness, continuing to fulfil the right of Allah that is upon him."
"3293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are my generation, then the second, then the third; then there will come people in whom there is no good."
"3294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them; then after them there will come people who will grow fat and love obesity, and who will give testimony before it is asked of them."
"3295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people are my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them; then there will come people whose testimony will precede his oath, and whose oath will precede his testimony."
"3296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of people is the one whose life is long and whose deeds are good."
"3297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of people is the one whose life is long and whose deeds are good, and the worst of people is the one whose life is long and whose deeds are bad."
"3298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best woman is the one who pleases her husband when he looks at her, obeys him when he gives a command, and does not oppose him in anything he dislikes concerning her own person and her wealth."
"3299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best woman is the one who pleases you when you look at her, obeys you when you give a command, and guards herself and your wealth in your absence."
"3300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best marriage is the one that is easiest."
"3301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of my Ummah is the generation in which I was sent, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then after them will come people who love obesity and who give testimony before their testimony is sought."
"3302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the people of the East are Abd al-Qays."
"3303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your dates is the Barni date; it removes illness and there is no illness in it."
"3304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your garments is white; clothe your living in it and shroud your dead in it."
"3305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your garments is white, so shroud your dead in it and clothe your living in it. And the best of your kohl is ithmid; it makes the hair grow and sharpens the eyesight."
"3306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the households of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar."
"3307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the households of the Ansar are Banu Abd al-Ashhal."
"3308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your religion is scrupulous piety (wara')."
"3309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your religion is that which is easiest."
"3310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the men's rows is the first row and the worst is the last row, and the best of the women's rows is the last row and the worst is the first row."
"3311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best prayer of women is in the innermost part of their homes."
"3312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you in Islam are those with the best character, provided they have understanding of the religion."
"3313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who are best in repaying debts."
"3314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who is best to his family, and I am the best of you to my family."
"3315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who is best to my family after me."
"3316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you are those who are best to women."
"3317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then after them there will be people who will betray and will not be regarded as trustworthy, who will give testimony though their testimony is not sought, who will make vows but not fulfil them, and obesity will appear among them."
"3318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who feeds others and returns the greeting of peace (salam)."
"3319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one who learned the Qur'an and taught it to others."
"3320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of you is the one from whom good is hoped and from whose evil people are safe, and the worst of you is the one from whom no good is hoped and from whose evil people are not safe."
"3321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of what people have been given is good character."
"3322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam; in it there is nourishment and healing from illness. And the worst water on the face of the earth is the water of the valley of Barhut in the region of Hadramawt; it is full of vermin like a swarm of locusts. In the morning it gushes forth, and by evening not a drop remains in it."
"3323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping (hijamah)."
"3324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and sea costus (al-qust al-bahri), and do not torment your children by pressing their throats to treat throat inflammation."
"3325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best places towards which riding animals are driven are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House (al-Bayt al-Atiq)."
"3326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best things a person leaves behind him are three: a righteous child who supplicates for him, an ongoing charity whose reward continues to reach him, and knowledge from which benefit is derived after him."
"3327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best place of prayer for women is the innermost part of their homes."
"3328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the women of the worlds are four: Maryam bint Imran, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Asiyah, the wife of Pharaoh."
"3329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of women who have ridden camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most tender towards a child in its infancy and the most careful in guarding a husband's property."
"3330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your women are those who bear many children, are loving, consoling and agreeable, provided they fear Allah. And the worst of your women are those who go out adorned and flaunting themselves and who are arrogant; they are the hypocrite women. None of them will enter Paradise except one as rare as the white-legged crow."
"3331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of its women is Maryam bint Imran, and the best of its women is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid."
"3332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best days on which to have cupping done are the seventeenth, the nineteenth and the twenty-first. And on the night of the Isra, I did not pass by any group of angels but that they said: 'O Muhammad, be sure to have cupping done.'"
"3333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On it Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on it he was admitted into Paradise, and on it he was expelled from it. And the Hour will not be established except on Friday."
"3334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On it Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on it he was sent down to the earth, on it his repentance was accepted, on it he died, and on it the Hour will be established. There is no creature on the face of the earth that does not listen attentively on Friday morning, out of fear of the Hour, until the sun rises, except the human being. And on that day there is a moment such that no believing servant who finds it while in prayer and asks Allah for something except that Allah will surely grant it to him."
"3335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was given the choice between intercession and half of my Ummah entering Paradise, and I chose intercession."
"3336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The trustworthy Muslim treasurer who gives what he has been commanded to give, in full and complete, willingly, and delivers it to the one for whom it was ordered, is also counted as one of the givers of charity."
"3337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The maternal uncle is an heir."
"3338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir."
"3339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The maternal aunt is of the status of the mother."
"3340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The maternal aunt is like a mother."
"3341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The caliphate in my Ummah after me will last thirty years, then after that there will be kingship."
"3342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The caliphate is in Quraysh, governance is in the Ansar, the call to prayer (adhan) is in the Abyssinians, and jihad and emigration (hijrah) are in the Muslims and the Muhajirun who come after them."
"3343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All of creation sends blessings upon the one who teaches goodness, even the fish of the sea."
"3344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wine is the root of all filthy things. Whoever drinks it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days, and if he dies while it is in his stomach, he dies the death of the Jahiliyyah."
"3345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wine is the root of all indecencies and the greatest of the major sins. Whoever drinks it may, in his intoxication, even assault his mother, his maternal aunt and his paternal aunt."
"3346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wine comes from these two trees: the date palm and the grapevine."
"3347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Khawarij are the dogs of Hell."
"3348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is a habit and evil is stubbornness, and whoever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."
"3349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and the one who spends on horses is like a person who keeps his hand open to give charity and never closes it."
"3350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Horses are of three kinds: a horse for the Most Merciful, a horse for Satan, and a horse for man. The horse of the Most Merciful is the one kept tethered in the path of Allah; its fodder, its dung and its urine will all be in his scale (of deeds). The horse of Satan is the one on which gambling or wagers are made. And the horse of man is the one a person keeps for the sake of breeding it, so it is a protection against poverty."
"3351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among horses, goodness lies in the forelocks of the reddish-brown ones."
"3352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Horses are for three kinds of people: for one man they are a reward, for another they are a means of protection, and for a third they are a burden of sin. The one for whom they are a reward is the man who tethers them in the path of Allah and leaves them a long rope to graze in a pasture or a garden; whatever they eat within the length of their rope from the pasture or garden becomes good deeds for him. And if their rope breaks and they run off over one or two rises, their tracks and their dung also become good deeds for him. And if they pass by a stream and drink water, even though he did not intend to water them, that too becomes good deeds for him. The second man is the one who tethers them for the sake of self-sufficiency, protection and chastity, and then does not forget the right of Allah concerning their necks and their backs; so they are a means of protection for him. And the third man is the one who tethers them out of pride, show and hostility towards the people of Islam; so they are a burden of sin for him."
"3353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, (that is,) reward and spoils of war."
"3354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"3355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are helped because of them. So stroke their forelocks, pray for blessing for them, and put collars on them, but do not put bowstring collars on them."
"3356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Goodness and blessing are tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are helped because of them. Put collars on them, and do not put bowstring collars on them."
"3357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tent (of Paradise) is a hollow pearl whose height into the sky is sixty miles. In each of its corners the believer will have family members whom the others (in the other corners) will not be able to see."
